  amazing spider-man series that we did  not get that third film here's the story  according to this book on how it all  happened so sony had really really big  plans for the amazing spider-man  franchise with andrew garfield and as a  lot of people know they were going to  make a third one however this all  changed the day amy pascal a producer  for spider-man met with kevin feige sony  wanted to do a lot with spider-man  however the sequel the amazing  spider-man 2 had just flopped and they  didn't really know what to do and they  were kind of in a panic especially if  you consider the fact that they had a  lot of spin-off series in the spider-man  universe happening but at the same time  kevin feige and marvel studios are  sitting over there crushing it with the  mcu like destroying the box offices plus  fans really love their movies so after  the amazing spider-man 2 sony decided  that they want to do that they want to  be as big as the mcu so amy pascal a  producer and chairperson over at sony  motion pictures group called over kevin  feige and here's the story according to  the book on how everything went down it  says with a good sense of how they would  like to handle the character feige was  ready for his lunch with pascal what he  wasn't ready for was pascal's reaction  to his proposal the meeting was in her  office at sony as expected pascal wasted  no time in expressing her strong desire  to have feige be more directly involved  creatively in the making of sony  pictures is the amazing spider-man 3.  excited about the ideas her team  currently had pascal said she would send  feige the latest draft about halfway  through the delicious sandwich that she  had brought in i said amy in all  fairness it's not gonna work shares  kevin feige you see what amy pascal  didn't know is that kevin feige had  plans and ideas of his own to go forward  with spider-man just not in sony's  universe you see what amy pascal did not  know is that kevin feige actually had  plans of his own for spider-man just not  in the sony universe in the mcu so after  kevin feige tells amy pascal in all  fairness it's not gonna work this is  what he says we've sort of done that  before and i don't think i'm  particularly helpful there but kevin  feige was not done he had a counter  proposal the only way i know how to do  anything is to just do it entirely so  why don't you let us do it don't think  of it as two studios and don't think of  it as giving another studio back the  rights no change of hands of money just  engage us to produce it just pretend  it's like what dc did with christopher  nolan i'm not saying we're nolan but i  am saying there is a production company  that is doing this pretty well just  engage the services of that production  company to make the movie and the  production company he is obviously  referring to is marvel studios and it  says here that pascal was taken back she  was super surprised and then she got  upset it says at first i was super  resentful she admits i think i started  crying and threw him out of my office or  threw a sandwich at him i'm not sure  which then she started to think it  through by the 5th spider-man movie we  weren't giving them anything new and i  have to be honest about it we were  trying so hard to be different we even  went into places to be different that we  shouldn't have we weren't fresh anymore  pascal continues the lucky thing is  kevin and i come from the same place in  terms of how we love peter i've been  working with kevin on spider-man movies  since sam raimi's he would come to the  meetings get everybody coffee and he  never said a word for years which makes  you love somebody because then when they  do open their mouth you realize that  they've been thinking all the big  thoughts and are really smart but never  had to hear themselves talk pascal  called feige back the next day after  their lunch the concept of a  collaboration between sony and marvel  studios had not left her mind after  hearing his specific thoughts on what to  do with spider-man in the mcu she admits  the idea of putting him up against a  world where everybody had everything and  he had nothing was a whole new way of  telling his story i thought gosh dang  that guy's smart and yeah he was and he  is really really smart he's the  president of marvel studios and i think  everybody could probably agree that  spider-man in the mcu is way better than  anything that sony could have produced  on their own now from there marvel  studios would sort of softly bring  spider-man into the mcu introducing him  in captain america civil war briefly  briefly but super iconically and also it  kind of makes you wonder because a lot  of us are wondering right now if they're  going to show the other two spider-man  toby maguire and andrew garfield in the  trailer if you think back to the civil  war trailers they actually showed  spider-man they showed his debut in the  trailers before the movie so there is  definitely a possibility that they could  do that for toby and andrew and of  course we know how it went civil war  homecoming spider-man far from home and  now spider-man no a home that could have  more hype than avengers end game this  movie has the potential to be the  biggest movie of all time if andrew and  toby are truly in it this movie is going  to destroy the box office it's just  simply going to be insane and people are  going to go back to the theaters and  re-watch this over and over and over  again i think i watched in-game like 10  times in the movie theater i'll probably  watch this movie more if toby and andrew  are in it in which of course a lot of us  are pretty dang sure i've had insiders  tell me that it's 100 sure a guaranteed  thing but of course we have to see but  spider-man actually really helped shape  the mcu obviously being one of the most  popular characters of all time if not  the most popular character multiverse of  badness and the whole concept of the  multiverse really shines when we're  talking about spider-man because it  opens the spider verse even if the other  two spider-man didn't come back we still  have the old villains from the other  universes this alone is enough for a ton  of people to want to go see this movie  and they are but that's the story of how  kevin feige went over to sony and got  spider-man in the mcu what a freaking  legend thank you kevin feige and thank  you sony for doing what you thought was  best for the character be sure to let me  know all of your thoughts about this in  the comments down below and don't forget  to subscribe and hit that notification  bell so you don't miss out on any of the  latest spider-man and mcu videos for  live updates you can follow me on  instagram and twitter and now tick-tock  and as always thank you all so much for  watching woof  you

